  "title": "Model routes gained new capabilities",
  "summary": "A week of broader model choices, more useful generation controls, and more places to see what people are building.\n\n`openai-large` moved to GPT-5.2, while `openai` moved to GPT-5 Mini and `openai-fast` stayed on Nano. Gemini requests gained built-in tools alongside function tools, with code execution, Google Search, and URL context used by default when no tools are supplied. Claude requests through Bedrock also gained working HTTP image URL input.\n\nSelf-hosted `zimage` joined image generation with 2× upscaling, and a follow-up corrected requested dimensions before upscaling. Flux now keeps four generation steps even when traffic rises. Generated images no longer carry a Pollinations logo, so the `nologo` flag went away too.\n\nChat gained image and video generation controls that travel with the request. The rebuilt Hello site brings image and text generation, a vision-capable model selector, community creations, and interactive API examples together. Model Monitor adds a view of model health, errors, traffic, success rates, and latency.\n\nNew listings span SDKs, Discord and Telegram bots, image studios, illustrated stories, games, stock-image preparation, and browser-based video production. It was a particularly busy week for examples of what a simple generation API becomes in other people's hands.",
